From: ascend-torchtitan
Subject: [PATCH] ops-nn: JIT builder must follow torch's required C++ standard

Cannot be filed upstream from here: ops-nn lives at gitcode.com/cann/ops-nn, and
this project's operating scope is gitcode.com/ascend only (P10). The fix is kept
here so the build stays reproducible and so whoever can file it has it ready.

Problem
  torch_extension/cann_ops_nn/op_builder/builder.py hard-codes "-std=c++17" in
  cxx_args(). torch's public headers have required C++20 since 2.9:

    torch/include/ATen/ATen.h:5:2: error: #error C++20 or later compatible
      compiler is required to use ATen.
    c10/util/intrusive_ptr.h: 'strong_ordering' in namespace 'std' does not name a type
    c10/util/TypeIndex.h: 'const string_view' has no member named 'starts_with'

  so every JIT-built op fails on torch >= 2.9 with "Failed to JIT compile
  operator 'situ_glu': Error building extension 'situ_glu'".

Fix
  Derive the standard from the installed torch (>= 2.9 -> c++20), with
  CANN_OPS_NN_CXX_STD as an override.

Verified
  torch 2.15.0.dev20260812 + torch_npu master, CANN 9.1.0, 910B2: situ_glu and
  situ_glu_grad build and register (torch.ops.cann_ops_nn.situ_glu present).

---
diff --git a/torch_extension/cann_ops_nn/op_builder/builder.py b/torch_extension/cann_ops_nn/op_builder/builder.py
index c983a676f..bfd478e56 100644
--- a/torch_extension/cann_ops_nn/op_builder/builder.py
+++ b/torch_extension/cann_ops_nn/op_builder/builder.py
@@ -131,11 +131,30 @@ class OpBuilder(ABC):
         )
         return paths
 
+    @staticmethod
+    def _cpp_std_flag():
+        """Match the C++ standard the installed torch requires.
+
+        torch's public headers use C++20 constructs (std::strong_ordering,
+        string_view::starts_with) since 2.9 and refuse to compile with
+        -std=c++17: "#error C++20 or later compatible compiler is required to
+        use PyTorch". Hard-coding c++17 therefore breaks every JIT-built op on a
+        current torch. CANN_OPS_NN_CXX_STD overrides the choice.
+        """
+        override = os.environ.get("CANN_OPS_NN_CXX_STD")
+        if override:
+            return f"-std={override}"
+        try:
+            major, minor = (int(p) for p in torch.__version__.split(".")[:2])
+        except ValueError:
+            return "-std=c++20"
+        return "-std=c++17" if (major, minor) < (2, 9) else "-std=c++20"
+
     def cxx_args(self):
         args = [
             "-O3",
             "-w",
-            "-std=c++17",
+            self._cpp_std_flag(),
             "-fPIC",
             "-fstack-protector-all",
             "-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now,-z,noexecstack",
